From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: PCI: host-common, dwc: Log why D3cold is vetoed

SL7 local: PCI: host-common, dwc: Log why D3cold is vetoed

During system suspend the DWC host driver keeps the link up and, in
qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq(), keeps a 1 kBps ALWAYS-tagged interconnect vote
and the PHY reference clock whenever pci_host_common_d3cold_possible()
returns false. On the Surface Laptop 7 this happens for the Wi-Fi and
NVMe controllers (1c08000.pci, 1bf8000.pci) and keeps the MC0, SH0 and
SH1 BCMs voted through suspend. Nothing reports which device vetoed the
power-off, so add pci_dbg() lines to the walk (device in a state other
than D3hot, or wakeup-enabled without PME from D3cold) and a dev_dbg()
in dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(). All of them are dynamic debug and silent by
default; enable them before suspend with

  echo 'file pci-host-common.c +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control
  echo 'file pcie-designware-host.c +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control
  echo 'file pci-driver.c +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control

No functional change.

Rationale: SL7 local diagnostic, needed to choose a safe fix for the
1 kBps suspend vote. Upstream-friendly as it stands.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
@@ -291,14 +291,18 @@
 	if (!pdev->dev.driver && !pci_is_enabled(pdev))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot)
+	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot) {
+		pci_dbg(pdev, "D3cold vetoed: device is in %s, not D3hot\n",
+			pci_power_name(pdev->current_state));
 		goto exit;
+	}
 
 	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev)) {
-		if (!pci_pme_capable(pdev, PCI_D3cold))
+		if (!pci_pme_capable(pdev, PCI_D3cold)) {
+			pci_dbg(pdev, "D3cold vetoed: wakeup enabled but no PME from D3cold\n");
 			goto exit;
-		else
-			*flags |= PCI_HOST_PME_D3COLD_CAPABLE;
+		}
+		*flags |= PCI_HOST_PME_D3COLD_CAPABLE;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -1229,8 +1229,10 @@
 	if (!dw_pcie_link_up(pci))
 		goto stop_link;
 
-	if (!pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(pci->pp.bridge, &pme_capable))
+	if (!pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(pci->pp.bridge, &pme_capable)) {
+		dev_dbg(pci->dev, "D3cold not possible, keeping the link up\n");
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (pci->pp.ops->pme_turn_off) {
 		pci->pp.ops->pme_turn_off(&pci->pp);
